1. **Define Variables:**
   Let the present age of Allen be \( x \) (in years) and the present age of his mother be \( y \) (in years).

2. **Set Up Equations:**
   We know from the problem statement that:
   \[
   \begin{cases}
   \text{Allen is 25 years younger than his mother:} \\
   \text{Allen's age in 3 years is 1-year older than his mother's age (since in 3 years, Allen will be } x+3 \text{ years old, and his mother will be } y+3 \text{ years old}:} \\
   \text{Thus, } x - y = 1 + 3 = 4 \quad \text{(1)}
   \end{cases}
   \]
   Also, given that the sum of their ages in 3 years will be 41:
   \[
   \begin{cases}
   x + y + 3 = 41 \quad \text{(2)}
   \end{cases}
   \]

3. **Solve the System of Equations:**
   We have two equations:
   \[
   \begin{cases}
   x - y = 4 \quad \text{(Equation 1)} \\
   x + y + 3 = 41 \quad \text{(Equation 2)}
   \end{cases}
   \]

4. **Subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2:

\[
4 \text{ trays} \times 25 \text{ gingerbreads/tray} = 100 \text{ gingerbreads}
\]
\[
3 \text{ trays} \times 20 \text{ gingerbreads/tray} = 60 \text{ gingerbreads}
\]
\[
100 \text{ gingerbreads} + 60 \text{ gingerbreads} = 160 \text{ gingerbreads}
\]

Thus, Diane bakes a total of 160 gingerbreads.
